      "text": "A valid broken-link condition must preserve P1 unloading and P2 inspection while removing only consumption of P1 arrivals. No allowed control can do this: the only destination is their shared rack and arrival establishes eligibility. Co-presence without that connection is likewise unavailable. Blocking unloading disables P1 output; withholding inspection disables P2 processing. Neither counts as link ablation."
